{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And Yosef gathered all the silver that was found, etc.</b> — Yosef brought the aforementioned silver, for in it he mentions 'all the silver.' And Scripture here proclaims the virtue of Yosef and his great faithfulness, for he brought everything into the king's treasury and acquired for him both the livestock and the land and also the bodies, and despite all this he found favor in the eyes of the people, for this was from HaShem." "<b>And by way of</b> the plain sense of the verses: this silver he gathered over five years and brought it to Pharaoh, for how is it possible that the silver and the livestock would be exhausted in a single year? Rather, the silver sufficed them for all five years, for so is the way of lands in a time of famine — they press and restrict themselves, and their silver and gold with them suffices them a long time. And Scripture mentions that after the silver was exhausted, at the end of five years they came to Yosef — and this was in the sixth year — and he gave them bread in exchange for their livestock, and he needed to guide them with it so that they would eat sparingly and not abundantly."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:20:55.408306859Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}